---
/* DRAFT-FOR-ED — candidate node page, /next preview namespace. */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import MarkNote from '../../components/MarkNote.astro'

export const prerender = true
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Handwriting pipeline"
  description="About a thousand handwritten notebook pages, parsed, transcribed, and made searchable."
>
  <article class="node">
    <p class="draft-stamp">draft · under review</p>
    <header data-mark="hw:masthead">
      <h1>Handwriting pipeline</h1>
      <p class="dek">A thousand notebook pages, written by hand, read by machines.</p>
      <p class="meta">craft · working · Supernote, Python, local models</p>
    </header>

    <section data-mark="hw:what">
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>
        The notebooks come first: daily pages written by hand on an e-ink tablet — about
        a thousand pages across dozens of notebooks so far. The pipeline pulls them off
        the device, parses the proprietary format, and hands each page to a vision model
        for transcription. The models run locally, on hardware in the house, so the
        journals never leave home.
      </p>
      <p>
        Choosing the transcription model was its own project: a structured bake-off ran
        three local vision models over the same eleven-page notebook against a frontier
        reference read. The winner transcribed every page cleanly and preserved the
        notebooks' own coined vocabulary — and the losing runs taught as much as the
        winner, including a failure mode where a model inserted a familiar term onto a
        page where it never appeared.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section data-mark="hw:why">
      <h2>Why handwriting</h2>
      <p>
        Writing by hand is slow on purpose. The page holds what existed before any
        machine touched it — language, drawings, wrong turns — and the pipeline's job is
        to make that record searchable without replacing it. The same conviction shaped
        the summer camp this year: students kept daily handwritten journals before
        anything was generated.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <MarkNote />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .node {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--page-gutter) var(--space-24);
  }
  .draft-stamp {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .dek {
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  p {
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
